From: =?UTF-8?q?Simon=20Z=C3=BCnd?= <szuend@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:26:19 +0000
Subject: [parser] Restore parse restriction when reparsing Function
 constructor top-level
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Move the Script::CompilationKind::kFunctionConstructor check into
UnoptimizedCompileFlags::SetFlagsForFunctionFromScript (guarded by
is_toplevel()) so that top-level
UnoptimizedCompileFlags::ForFunctionCompile also sets
ONLY_SINGLE_FUNCTION_LITERAL.

Also use parsing_dynamic_function_declaration_ for the eager compile
hint in Parser::ParseFunctionLiteral, and check that syntax_kind and
kind match when matching an existing SharedFunctionInfo to a
FunctionLiteral.

R=verwaest@chromium.org

Fixed: 568831099
Change-Id: Ie918dad4ee60ccbeb3d403e293d4802ba8123f2a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8523457
Reviewed-by: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Simon Zünd <szuend@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110345}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): This branch's UnoptimizedCompileFlags::ForScriptCompile has no set_outer_language_mode() line; the parse-restriction move is otherwise identical. Parser::ParseFunctionLiteral keeps this branch's local params_need_validation (upstream's parsing_dynamic_function_declaration_ member does not exist here; same value).

